  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=2t+\\sqrt{t}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\u2016f(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9 & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+\\sqrt{t})^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+4t\\sqrt{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{8{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t}}{5}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{103}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\u2016f(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\\frac{103}{30}}.\n$$",
